        heading: "Product-Level Value Chain Analytics",
        body: "PoS data enables value chain eficiencia análisis at the individual product level, revealing heterogeneity that aggregate commodity-level análisis conceals. Different varieties of the same crop may travel through different value chains with different eficiencia characteristics: locally grown heritage varieties may reach minorista through short, efficient chains, while improved varieties produced in distant regions pass through longer chains with higher accumulated margens. Processed versus unprocessed versions of the same agricultural product exhibit different spread dynamics: the margen on raw tomatoes reflects primarily transport and minorista costos, while the margen on tomato sauce additionally incorporates processing, packaging, and branding costos, each of which may contribute differently to overall value chain eficiencia or ineficiencia. PoS product-level data can distinguish between minoristaer margen and upstream margen contributions to the total spread by comparing minorista prices across different store types selling the same products—if supermarkets and independent grocers charge different prices for identical products, the difference reflects minoristaer-level margen variation rather than upstream cadena de suministro characteristics. Platforms like askbiz.co that aggregate product-level pricing across diverse minorista formats provide the data breadth needed for this decomposition, enabling identification of whether value chain ineficiencia concentrates at the minorista level, the wholesale level, or in the farm-to-first-buyer segment.",
